  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Roma Education Fund (REF) 2015-2021 - Roma Education Fund (REF) 2015-2020</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Roma Education Fund (REF) 2015-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">REFs, d.v.s. Roma Education Funds, verksamhet syftar till att h&#xf6;ja utbildningsniv&#xe5;n f&#xf6;r romer i Europa. Sida avser ge k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till REF, vars  verksamhet  best&#xe5;r i att genom projektbidrag, stipendier, forskning och p&#xe5;verkansarbete &#xf6;ka antalet romer som f&#xe5;r kvalitativ utbildning fr&#xe5;n f&#xf6;rskola &#xe4;nda upp till doktorsgrad. Sida avser finansiera verksamhet i alla de ODA-klassade l&#xe4;nder som REF &#xe4;r verksamt i, d.v.s. i Albanien, Bosnien Herzegovina, Kosovo, Makedonien, Montenegro, Serbien, Turkiet, Moldavien och Ukraina. Sida har i flera &#xe5;r gett projektst&#xf6;d till REF men bed&#xf6;mer nu att REF som organisation &#xe4;r mogen att hantera k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d. REFs kapacitet att hantera medel p&#xe5; ett ansvarsfullt s&#xe4;tt samt organisationens f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att bedriva sin verksamhet g&#xf6;r att Sida bed&#xf6;mer den sammantagna risken f&#xf6;r insatsen vara l&#xe5;g.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Roma Education Fund, REF, aims at increasing the level of Education   of Europe&apos;s Roma population. Through the means of providing project   grants, scholarships and through research and policy work REF         contributes to increase the number of Roma achieving qualitative      education at all levels in the education cycle, from pre-school to    post-graduate studies.

Distribution:
No country allocations in advance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To close the gap in educational outcomes between Roma and non-Roma. REF contributes to SDG 4 -&#xa0;ensure inclusive and equitable quality education and promote lifelong learning opportunities for all.
The REF strategic framework 2021 - 2030 sets out three strategic orientations:
i) supporting individual beneficiaries,ii) utilizing/sensitizing education systems through advocating the needs and interests of Roma,iii) making REF a specialised organisation for the mobilization of the human potential of Roma and their contribution pedagogy.</narrative>
  </description>
